config RUST_MPROTECT
	bool "Use Rust memory protection and protection-key operations"
	depends on RUST && MMU
	depends on !RANDSTRUCT && !GCC_PLUGIN_LATENT_ENTROPY && !CFI
	default y
	help
	  Build mprotect.o from Rust with configured native layouts and ABI.
	  The PTE through PGD protection walks, batch/sub-batch decisions,
	  userfaultfd and NUMA protections, VMA accounting and permission
	  changes, and mprotect/pkey syscall bodies execute in Rust.
	  Native leaves retain architecture/header operations and syscall
	  metadata. The original mprotect.c is preserved as reference only.
	  Native compiler policy checks must pass before build admission.
